The Emotion Quote App is a simple yet creative web application built using Python Flask and HTML/CSS, designed to display meaningful quotes based on the user’s selected emotion. The idea behind this project is to create a lightweight, interactive, and visually appealing tool that helps users express and understand their feelings through powerful words. Whether someone is feeling happy, sad, motivated, stressed, or simply wants inspiration, the app provides a relevant quote instantly.
This application uses a minimal backend powered by Flask, making it easy to run, edit, and deploy. The frontend includes a clean and responsive interface, ensuring a smooth user experience across desktops and mobile devices. The UI focuses on clarity and accessibility, allowing users to select an emotion with a simple click and immediately receive a quote that matches their mood. You can also customize and expand the app by adding more emotions or modifying the list of quotes directly in the code.
You are welcome to fork this repository, improve the UI, add more features, or integrate APIs for dynamic quote fetching. Contributions are always appreciated!
